# webOS image rendering (hard-won in v0.0.58–v0.0.66)

Target engine is old Chromium on LG TVs (browserslist: Chrome 53). Two real
bugs cost many releases; do not reintroduce them.

## 1. Never hand a full-size poster bitmap to the compositor

The webOS compositor cannot rasterize very large source images (hi-res `wide`
posters). The frame containing the raw `<img>` never activates: the screen
freezes on the previous frame (spinner appears stuck) until a real key press
forces a redraw. JS stays alive — only the picture is missing.

**Symptom fingerprint:** spinner "freezes", poster appears the instant any
button is pressed, worse on sharper/bigger posters. This is a compositor
stall, NOT a JS deadlock, NOT a load/decode-event problem.

**The working fix** (keep this architecture):
- `useDecodedImage` (src/hooks/useDecodedImage.ts) preloads the image off-DOM
  (`new Image()`), with retries and a safety timeout. `img.decode()` is used
  only where it exists (Chrome 64+ / webOS 5+).
- The banner mounts only after the preload finishes — the DOM mutation itself
  schedules the repaint webOS otherwise drops.
- The poster is drawn **downscaled onto a screen-sized `<canvas>`**
  (`drawBannerCover` in src/screens/ItemScreen.tsx), so the compositor only
  ever sees a ~1920×1080 bitmap. Small card thumbnails are fine as `<img>`.

## 2. Things that were tried and do NOT work

- `revealWhenDecoded` / gating visibility on `onload` + `img.decode()`
  callbacks — flaky on webOS, leaves the image at `opacity: 0`.
- Force-paint hacks: `translateZ(0)` toggles, opacity nudges, `setInterval`
  repaint loops, clearing/reassigning `src` on stall timers.
- Mounting `<img>` early and waiting: no DOM change after load ⇒ no repaint.
- Synchronous `canvas.drawImage` decode of a huge JPEG in `onload` blocks the
  Chrome 53 main thread; avoid off-screen sync decodes of full-size posters.

## 3. Canvas banner details

- The canvas backing store is fixed at mount; keep `object-fit: cover` on
  `.item-banner-image` so layout shifts (expanding side menu) crop instead of
  squishing the frame.
- `object-fit`/`object-position` do not apply to canvas *content* — the
  cover-crop (incl. the `center 18%` vertical bias) is baked in by
  `drawBannerCover`.

## 4. Side menu expand ≠ window resize

Expanding the side menu shrinks `.app-with-menu` without firing `window.resize`,
and Chrome 53 has no `ResizeObserver`. Grids that cache `itemsPerRow` /
`cardWidth` (esp. `VirtualGrid` totalHeight) then keep a too-small height and
sections overlap (History movies over series).

Fix: `SideMenu` dispatches `kpuppy-content-resize`; `useGridLayout` listens;
`VirtualGrid` resets measured row height when layout inputs change.
